   "columns": [
    [
     {
      "type": "textmedia",
      "header": "<h1> FAQ </h1>",
      "body": "<p class=\"large-text\">Frequently Asked Questions</p>",
      "images": [],
      "videos": [],
      "pos": "text",
      "cols": 1,
      "valign": "top",
      "ftype": "text",
      "id": "c3794",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "type": "accordion",
      "header": "",
      "items": [
       {
        "title": "What is webTMS?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>ZOLLER-webTMS TMS Tool Management Solutions is the web version of the TMS desktop application, which can be used on various devices. Since ZOLLER-webTMS was developed from the ground up, not all modules and functions of the TMS desktop version are currently available.</p> <p>Advantages of a web application: No installation is required on devices. Any device with a browser (PC, smartphone, tablet, laptop, etc.) can access webTMS immediately. Installation, configuration, and maintenance are performed only on the host device, which significantly reduces administrative overhead.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3791",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "What is webTMS StartUp Edition?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The webTMS StartUp Edition is the first version of webTMS to be released. It comes pre-installed on all presetting and measuring machines as well as TMS hardware products (»keeper«, »autoLock«, »toolOrganizer«, »zTower«, »toolStation«, »cockpit«), so customers can get started immediately. </p> <p>As soon as the device has a network connection, simply start webTMS. From that point on, the software can be used on any device with a browser without any additional installation.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3915",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Can TMS customers also use the webTMS StartUp Edition?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>This version of webTMS is not compatible with TMS because it is hosted on the IPC of the presetting and measuring machine or on a TMS hardware product that is not designed for this dual use. Using both systems simultaneously can lead to performance issues and crashes. </p> <p>A compatible on-premises version (in beta) that is installed and hosted on the customer’s server is currently under development.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3917",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "How do I install or set up webTMS?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>No installation is required, as webTMS is already preinstalled on the presetting and measuring machine or a TMS hardware product. You only need to create a trial license (or select a purchased license) and start webTMS on the device that should serve as the host. Optionally, you can configure the database, graphic, and document path.</p> <p>To allow access from other devices, the presetting and measuring machine or a TMS hardware product must be connected to the network. Access is via the standard ports 80 and 443.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3921",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "How can a customer purchase or extend a license?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Currently, customers can contact their ZOLLER representative to request a customized quote. The license is sent manually by the software deployment team, but this process will be automated in the future. Going forward, customers will be able to use MYZOLLER for this purpose. Customers can choose between monthly, semi-annual, or annual billing with a minimum term of one year.</p> <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/ca/company/contact\">Contact us now</a></p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c3919",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "ftype": "accordion",
      "id": "c3793",
